From 81e4cb015d0ae9e6daf4c549726fcf3001e1359e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:54:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(turning): the workholding rpm limit judges the work
 spindle, not a live tool's speed

The chuck / collet limit (#1031) used spindle_law::turns, which also
counts the cross drill (a driven radial tool, the work held still), so
a 10000 rpm cross drill was refused under a 100 rpm chuck with the
false text "turns the work at 10000 rpm". The program gate now sorts
each section by which spindle its S drives, as the lathe post does:
turning and the lathe's axial drill turn the work at the stated rpm
(G97 refused above the limit; the G96 clamp unchanged); a C-axis
live-tool section (moves state C) turns the work only on C, judged by
the machine's C rate (refused by name when that is over the limit or
unstated while a limit is stated); a cross drill is not judged.

Fixes #1174

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
